
Soft Link (Symbolic Link) : A soft link is like a shortcut to another file.
=========================

# Create it with:
ln -s original.txt softlink.txt


# Example:
original.txt
     ↑
     |
softlink.txt

# If you run: cat softlink.txt
Linux follows the link and reads original.txt.


# Check it:
ls -l

# You might see:
-rw-r--r-- 1 user user 100 Aug 16 original.txt
lrwxrwxrwx 1 user user  12 Aug 16 softlink.txt -> original.txt

The l at the beginning means it is a symbolic link.


Important characteristics
=========================
Can link to a file or directory
Can point to a file on a different filesystem
Has its own inode
If the original file is deleted, the soft link becomes broken
Can point to another soft link

